# Rat Growth Mixed-Design Repeated Measures ANOVA

## Project Title
**BIO2105 - Biostatistics Formative Assessment 11: Mixed-Design Repeated Measures ANOVA Using R**

**Authors:** Chavez, Ishi Santi V. | Lagaña, Alyssa Kaye L. | Quillope, Arabela Renee Florence M. (Section 4)

## Research Objectives
The primary objective of this study is to evaluate whether rat body weight differs significantly across three experimental treatment groups (**Control**, **Thiouracil**, and **Thyroxin**) and across five weekly measurement occasions (**Week 0 to Week 4**)[cite: 1]. Specifically, this analysis investigates whether the pattern of body weight change over time depends on the treatment administered (**Treatment × Time Interaction**)[cite: 1].

## Dataset Description
The dataset (`rats`) is sourced from the `nlmm` R package and originates from the classic growth curve experiment by Box (1950)[cite: 1]. 
- **Sample Size:** 27 rats (10 Control, 10 Thiouracil, 7 Thyroxin—three rats were removed from the Thyroxin group following an accident) totaling 135 observations[cite: 1].
- **Variables:**
  - `id`: Individual rat identifier (Nominal / Subject ID)
  - `trt`: Between-subjects factor (`Control`, `Thiouracil`, `Thyroxin`)
  - `time`: Within-subjects factor (`Week 0` through `Week 4`)
  - `y`: Dependent variable representing body weight in grams (Continuous)

